From b8fc1d5a6912789d7daca9171fa1746695ef492e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neil Horman <nhorman@openssl.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 09:25:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Increase BIO_dgram_pair ring buffer size on AIX for quic
 tests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AIX has a unique definition of struct sockaddr_un (AF_UNIX addresses).
Whereas most unixes define the structure to have a sun_path field of 108
bytes, AIX defines sun_path to be an array of 1023 bytes.  Because
BIO_dgram_pairs use two BIO_ADDR's (which are a union containing
sockaddr_un) to define a pseudo UDP header, any dgram pair with a fixed
ring buffer size is likely to be unable to transmit a complete frame if
the ring buffer is sized with less than sizeof(BIO_ADDR)*2 + 1200 bytes
allocated on AIX.

Fix it by increasing the ring buffer size for such tests

Fixes #32506

Reviewed-by: Saša Nedvědický <sashan@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Norbert Pocs <norbertp@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Andrew Dinh <andrewd@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Thu Oct  1 19:13:27 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/32838
(cherry picked from commit 7ef69a722c129fe446d7a1fef52ff8f12ccb010b)
---
 test/helpers/quictestlib.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test/helpers/quictestlib.c b/test/helpers/quictestlib.c
index c73431338d9e..9822b2a4b7b7 100644
--- a/test/helpers/quictestlib.c
+++ b/test/helpers/quictestlib.c
@@ -1446,6 +1446,7 @@ static int create_dgram_pair(BIO **c_bio_p, BIO **s_bio_p)
     struct in_addr ina;
     int bio_flags = 0;
     int ok;
+    size_t ring_buf_size = 1500;
 
     ina.s_addr = htonl(0x7f000001);
     bio_flags |= BIO_DGRAM_CAP_HANDLES_DST_ADDR
@@ -1455,7 +1456,16 @@ static int create_dgram_pair(BIO **c_bio_p, BIO **s_bio_p)
 
     c_bio = NULL;
     s_bio = NULL;
-    ok = BIO_new_bio_dgram_pair(&c_bio, 1500, &s_bio, 1500);
+#if defined(_AIX)
+    /*
+     * AIX has a struct sockaddr_un definition that greatly inflates the size of the
+     * BIO_ADDR structure, two of which are used to form a pseudo udp header in bio
+     * dgram pair BIO's.  We need to increase the size of the pair ring buffers here
+     * to prevent test failures stemming from inability to transmit such large headers
+     */
+    ring_buf_size = 4096;
+#endif
+    ok = BIO_new_bio_dgram_pair(&c_bio, ring_buf_size, &s_bio, ring_buf_size);
     if (ok == 0) {
         TEST_info("%s BIO_new_bio_dgram_pair() error", OPENSSL_FUNC);
         goto done;
